prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a city delivery truck game. Load the milk truck model and navigate through a grid-based city to 5 delivery points to complete the delivery task.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import through ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/CesiumMilkTruck.glb;
(2) After loading is complete, place the truck at the starting position in the lower-left corner of the city and scale it appropriately;
(3) CesiumMilkTruck may contain wheel animations; play them using AnimationMixer;
(4) After loading is complete, set window.__3D_STATE__.modelLoaded = true;

[City Construction]
(5) Build a grid-based city with at least 5x5 blocks:
  a) Roads: gray PlaneGeometry strips approximately 3 units wide, forming a grid-based road system;
  b) Buildings: place BoxGeometry objects of different sizes at the center of the blocks, with random heights from 2-8 and random colors, serving as impassable buildings;
  c) Leave road intersections unobstructed;
(6) Mark 5 delivery points with glowing green cylinders (CylinderGeometry + MeshBasicMaterial, color: 0x00ff00, transparent, opacity 0.6), placed at different road positions, with a rotating green halo animation at the base;

[Truck Controls]
(7) WASD controls:
  a) W: accelerate forward in the direction the truck is facing;
  b) S: move toward the rear of the truck (brake/reverse);
  c) A: turn left (rotate the truck's heading);
  d) D: turn right;
(8) The truck has a maximum speed limit of approximately 5 units/second, with acceleration/deceleration inertia;
(9) When the keys are released, the truck naturally decelerates due to friction;

[Collision System]
(10) The truck must not pass through buildings; use AABB collision detection;
(11) When the truck collides with a building, it stops and rebounds slightly, and window.__3D_STATE__.collisionCount++;
(12) When a building is hit, that building flashes red for 0.3 seconds;

[Delivery Logic]
(13) When the truck enters the range of a delivery point (distance<2):
  a) The delivery point marker changes from green to blue (completed);
  b) window.__3D_STATE__.deliveries++;
  c) Play a simple particle/scaling confirmation animation;
(14) When all 5 delivery points have been completed, display the total time and rating;

[Timer]
(15) Timing starts when the truck moves for the first time;
(16) Timing stops after all deliveries have been completed;

[Camera]
(17) Use an overhead camera at an angle of approximately 45 degrees that follows the truck's movement;
(18) Optional: display a minimap in the lower-right corner showing a global overhead view, rendered to a small canvas using another orthographic camera;

[HUD Display]
(19) The HUD panel in the upper-left corner displays:
  - Delivery progress (id="deliveries", format "2/5");
  - Truck position (id="truckPos");
  - Current speed (id="speed");
  - Elapsed time (id="timer");
  - Collision count (id="collisionCount");
  - Model loading status (id="loadStatus");

[Visual Effects]
(20) Use a light gray-blue scene background (0xb0c4de);
(21) Use a DirectionalLight to simulate sunlight, plus an AmbientLight;
(22) Buildings cast shadows onto the roads (renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true);

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean (whether model loading is complete)
  - deliveries: number (number of completed deliveries, 0-5)
  - truckPosition: {x, y, z} (truck position)
  - speed: number (current speed)
  - timer: number (elapsed time in seconds)
  - collisionCount: number (number of collisions)
  - gameStarted: boolean (whether the game has started)
  - gameFinished: boolean (whether all deliveries have been completed)
  - deliveryPoints: Array<{x,z,completed:boolean}> (status of the 5 delivery points)

Output a single HTML file. Place this file in the same directory as the assets/ folder and run it through a local HTTP server.
